	)
	(text "Net classes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 207.01 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9cb496c7-b3c7-5d17-a427-3d9c3d15b6be")
	)
	(text "Order per power-circuit-design §2: connector -> fuse -> reverse-polarity element -> clamp and bulk -> loads.\nF101 0451003.MRL: 3 A fast, 125 V; breaking capacity per Littelfuse 451 datasheet; HW-PWR-002.\nQ101 CSD18543Q3A in the return (low-side N-FET, SLVA139 option 3, D-003): VDS 60 V, RDS(on) 8.1 mOhm at 10 V\n  (SLPS532 Table). Body diode conducts first, then R101 lifts the gate; D102 15 V Zener holds VGS <= 15 V\n  (abs max +-20 V) at 30 V in: (30-15)/100k = 0.15 mA. At 8 V in VGS = 8 V > 4.5 V RDS(on) point.\n  Reversed input: gate below source, Q101 off. Conducts both ways when on, so regeneration returns to the source.\nD101 SMAJ33A: VRWM 33 V >= 30 V max input; VC 53.3 V at IPP 7.5 A (Littelfuse SMAJ table, HW-PWR-003).\n  Ladder under VC: DRV8711 VM 60 V, CSD18543Q3A 60 V, LMR36510 VIN 70 V abs; 50 V capacitors are the weak\n  rung (C201, C301, C303-C305): accepted deviation D-004, checked by simulation S1 before release.\nVM_SENSE (R102/R103, placed at the ADC pin): 30 V reads 2.73 V; at the 53.3 V clamp 4.85 V through 100k is\n  12 uA into the pin, inside the -5/+5 mA injection limit (AN4899). 9.1 kOhm source: long ADC sample time.\nVM bulk (C301 100u) and HF bypass sit at the bridges, sheet 3 (power-pcb-layout §3.9).\nCaveat (D-003): board GND joins the USB host's ground; a reversed 24 V supply sharing that ground is not blocked."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 163.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bd92ffdc-963c-555e-954e-177073333cfa")
	)
